nal rule, }{\i\fs24 spells selected from a minor sphere of access are treated as if they were one level higher for spell point costs}{\fs24 . For example, a priest with minor access to the sphere of healing could select }{\i\fs24 cure light wounds}{\fs24 
, but the spell would cost him 6 SPs instead of 4; see the Table 29: Spell Point Costs for Major and Minor Spheres.
