\par Regardless of the character\rquote s actual level, his casting level is based on how long he has actually been able to use spells. A 9th\_level paladin is considered a 1st\_level caster for all level\_based variables that are part of a
 spell description. This level of ability increases as the paladin continues to advance, reaching a maximum of 9th level when the paladin reaches 17th level.
