\par \tab This nefarious spell affects the victim\rquote s life energies, increasing any fatigue or exhaustion the victim currently possesses. Alert and well\_rested charact
ers suddenly become tired and sluggish, and characters who are already fatigued may be reduced to near\_helplessness. In effect, the }{\i\fs24 ray }{\fs24 adds one level of fatigue or encumbrance to the victim. Moderately encumbered characters suffer a 
\endash 1 penalty to attack rolls; heavily encumbered characters suffer a \endash 2 penalty to attacks rolls and a +1 Armor Class penalty; and severely encumbered characters suffer a \endash 
4 penalty to attack rolls and a +3 Armor Class penalty. (Assume that monsters suffer a \endash 1 penalty to their attack rolls and reduce their movement rates by 33%.) The victim is allowed a saving throw to negate the spell\rquote s effects.
\par \tab If you are using the fatigue rules from the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote s Option\'99: Combat & Tactics }{\fs24 book, this spell operates in a slightly different manner\emdash 
fresh characters become fatigued, gaining one level of encumbrance; fatigued characters become exhausted, gaining two levels of encumbrance; and exhausted characters collapse in a quivering heap, unable to move or attack.
