\par Sensory: Small visual\tab Critical: Moderate (1 hit) slashing
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell makes a single weapon incredibly sharp by reducing one of its physical dimensions to an infinitesimal measurement. The }{\i\fs24 dimensional blade }{\fs24 
can slash through matter with as much effort as it takes to wave a stick through the air. Even stone and iron can be carved to pieces with ease. The spell can be cast on almost any hand\_held slashing (type S) weapon, as well as a 
few thrown weapons of this type, such as the chakram, shuriken, or a hand axe.
\par \tab Against creatures, the }{\i\fs24 dimensional blade }{\fs24 ignores any portion of Armor Class derived from armor itself; only magical and Dexterity adjustments affect the opponent\rquote s AC. For example, a warrior in }{\i\fs24 chain mail +2 }{
\fs24 with a Dexterity of 17 is normally AC 0, but against the dimensional blade he only applies the 3\_point adjustment for Dexterity and the 2\_point magical adjustment, for a total AC of 5. Creatures wearing purely magical armor (such as }{\i\fs24 
bracers of defense}{\fs24 ) may keep the full magical adjustment. Monsters with thick or toughened hides, such as dragons, may lose part of the Armor Class at the DM\rquote 
s discretion. The weapon gains a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls in any event, but the wielder ignores any Strength\_based combat adjustments\emdash muscle power doesn\rquote t help the blade at all.
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 dimensional blade }{\fs24 is also quite effective against inanimate objects. Any object with a diameter or thickness smaller than the blade\rquote s length must make 
a saving throw vs. disintegration when struck, or be cleanly severed in twain. Larger objects can be sawed through or sliced away at the rate of about 5 cubic feet per round. It\rquote s dangerous to attempt to disarm a }{\i\fs24 dimensional blade}{\fs24 
; the weapon used must make an item saving throw vs. disintegration or be destroyed.
\par \tab Finally, the blade is also effective against phased or ethereal creatures since part of its existence is forced into the Ethereal Plane. If the wielder has some way to detect creatures concealed i
n this way, the blade can strike and affect them normally, but without the power to negate Armor Class or other combat bonuses.
\par \tab The wizard must touch the weapon to be affected by the spell, but afterward anyone may wield it. The material component for this spell is a razor\_thin shard of glass.
\par 
