\par }{\fs28\cf6 Seven-Eyes
\par }{\b\fs24 (Abjuration, Conjuration/Summoning)
\par }{\fs24 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx3240\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\adjustright {\fs24 Range: 0\tab Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 rd./level\tab Casting Time: 7
\par Area of Effect: Create 7 eyes\tab Saving Throw: Special
\par Subtlety: +5\tab Knockdown: Varies
\par Sensory: Medium visual\tab Critical: Varies
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell conjures into existence seven magical orbs that float above the caster\rquote s head in a ring about 5 feet in diameter. The eyes remain for 1 round per level, or until the caster chooses to either expend the orb by using it in atta
ck or defense. In addition, as long as at least one eye is still in existence, the caster gains 360\'b0 vision and can }{\i\fs24 detect invisibility }{\fs24 and }{\i\fs24 detect phase }{\fs24 at will, with a 60\_
foot range. The powers of each eye are described below.
\par 
\par  \tab }{\b\fs24 Eye of the Mind. }{\fs24 This orb protects the caster against mental attack, charm, or influence, including }{\i\fs24 charm, beguiling, hold}{\fs24 , and }{\i\fs24 emotion }{\fs24 
effects. The first such attack is negated by the orb and destroys it in turn. If the wizard desires, the eye of the mind can instead be used to }{\i\fs24 charm person }{\fs24 like the 1st\_level wizard spell, although this also expends the orb.
\par  \tab }{\b\fs24 Eye of the Sword.}{\fs24  This eye deflects the first physical attack that endangers the caster, including hand\_held or missile attacks, and then disappears. The wizard can also emp
loy the eye of the sword to create five magical blades that strike as }{\i\fs24 magic missiles }{\fs24 for 1d4+1 points of damage each. (Knockdown d6, medium (1 hit) impact)
\par  \tab }{\b\fs24 Eye of the Mage. }{\fs24 One manifestation of raw energy, such as lightning, fire, force, cold, or a similar effect, is absorbed by the eye of the mage. The eye can also project a 60\_foot long by 5\_foot wide }{\i\fs24 lightning bolt }{
\fs24 that inflicts 4d8 damage (saving throw vs. spell for half damage) to all in its path. Either use expends the eye\rquote s power. (Knockdown d12, large (1\endash 3 hits) electricity)
\par  \tab }{\b\fs24 Eye of Venom. }{\fs24 This eye can be used to halt any one attack or effect that could poison the caster. In the case of an attacker armed with an envenomed weapon, the caster may decide to expend either the eye of venom or the eye o
f swords in order to block the attack. The eye can also be used to poison one creature within 30 feet; the victim must make a saving throw vs. poison or die in one round.
\par  \tab }{\b\fs24 Eye of the Spirit.}{\fs24  The first attack that affects the victim\rquote s life energy, including }{\i\fs24 energy drain, strength drain, cause wounds, trap the soul, magic jar}{\fs24 , or }{\i\fs24 death }{\fs24 
is parried by the eye of the spirit. The wizard may instead choose to expend the eye\rquote s power by casting }{\i\fs24 enervation }{\fs24 (see the 4th\_level wizard spell) upon one target within 30 feet.
\par  \tab }{\b\fs24 Eye of Artifice. }{\fs24 This eye deflects and is destroyed by the first attack directed at the caster from a magical device. If the attack also takes a form that may be blocked by another eye (for example, the bolt from a }{\i\fs24 
wand of lightning}{\fs24 ) the caster may choose which eye is expended. If used to attack instead, the eye of artifice functions as a }{\i\fs24 dispel magic }{\fs24 cast at 8th level.
\par  \tab }{\b\fs24 Eye of Stone. }{\fs24 This eye offers protection against the first attack that could petrify the caster and then vanishes. It can also be expended to cast }{\i\fs24 hold person}{\fs24 .
\par 
\par \tab Although any number of eyes can defend the wizard in the course of a single round, only one eye may be used to attack per round. When the caster uses an eye to attack, he may not cast a spell, attack physically, or employ an
other magical item in the same round; willing the eye to discharge its energies requires his complete concentration. Eye attacks are considered to have an initiative modifier of 1 or a speed of very fast in the }{\i\fs24 Player\rquote 
s Option: Combat & Tactics }{\fs24 initiative system.
\par \tab The material component is seven blessed gemstones worth at least 50 gold pieces each.
\par 
