\par Range: 10 yds./level\tab Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level\tab Casting Time: 6
\par Area of Effect: Special\tab Saving Throw: None
\par Subtlety: +4\tab Knockdown: d8
\par Sensory: Moderate visual\tab Critical: Medium (1 hit) 
\par \tab   slashing
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell summons a minor spirit or entity to the caster\rquote s aid. Clerics usually summon minor elementals of some kind, while shamans typically conjure an animal spirit or spirit of nature. Regardless of the spirit\rquote 
s origin, it appears as a ghostly beast of some kind\emdash wolves, bears, tigers, or lions are most common. The }{\i\fs24 animal spirit }{\fs24 obe
ys the mental commands of the priest, attacking his enemies or performing any other task that it could reasonably accomplish. The creature is incorporeal and cannot handle or manipulate objects of any kind, but it can see and hear as a normal animal of it
s archetype and could be used to scout a dangerous area or act as a distraction of some kind.
\par \tab In combat, the }{\i\fs24 animal spirit }{\fs24 has the following statistics: MV 24; AC 4; THAC0 15; Dmg 2d4. It can only be injured by magical weapons and can strike monsters hit o
nly by +1 or better weapons. The spirit has a number of hit points equal to 10 plus the caster\rquote s level, so a 6th\_level priest conjures a animal spirit with 16 hit points. The creature is not affected by }{\i\fs24 charm, sleep, hold, }{\fs24 
or other mind\_affecting spells and suffers no damage from cold\_based attacks. However, it is vulnerable to }{\i\fs24 dispel magic }{\fs24 or turning as an undead monster of the caster\rquote s Hit Dice. If the }{\i\fs24 animal spirit }{\fs24 
is turned, destroyed, or dispelled, the priest who summoned it must make a saving throw vs. spell or be stunned for 1d4 rounds.
\par \tab Because the spirit is intelligent and free\_willed under the caster\rquote s direction, the priest need not concentrate in order to direct its attacks\emdash an }{\i\fs24 animal spirit }{\fs24 could be ordered to attack a spellcaster in the back of 
an enemy party, while the cleric waded into hand\_to\_hand combat. The }{\i\fs24 animal spirit }{\fs24 
makes use of flank or rear attacks when it can and gains any normal combat bonuses that a living creature in its position would be entitled to. The priest enjoys instantaneous, silent communication with the }{\i\fs24 animal spirit }{\fs24 
and can order it to stop attacking, to change its target, or to undertake almost any conceivable action desired. However, the spirit must remain within the spell\rquote s range; if it is ever more than 10 yards per 
caster level away from the priest, it dissipates harmlessly.
\par \tab The material component is a small whistle carved from a bone taken from the appropriate type of animal.
\par 
