\par \tab This spell allows the priest to exert fine control over air currents and winds, possibly extinguishing small fires or manipulating light objects as he sees fit within the spell\rquote 
s range. Generally, the priest is limited to one discrete action per round since he must focus his wind servant tightly on any given task. The }{\i\fs24 wind servant }{\fs24 
can affect objects or creatures weighing up to 1 pound per caster level, twice as much if the obje
ct is reasonably light or airy (a cloak, scroll, or haystack, for instance), or 10 times as much if the object is designed to be carried by the wind, such as a ship\rquote s sail or a bird in flight.
\par \tab If an object is within the spell\rquote s weight limit, the caster may direct the }{\i\fs24 wind servant }{\fs24 to carry it along in gusts and air currents at a flying movement rate of 12 (E). If the object leaves the limits of the spell\rquote 
s range, the }{\i\fs24 wind servant }{\fs24 fails, and the object drops or falls normally from that point. Flying creature
s of size M or smaller can be forced to land or be driven away by use of the spell if they fall within the weight limit, or slowed by 50% if they exceed the weight limit. Employing the }{\i\fs24 wind servant }{\fs24 
against an arrow or light missile adds a penalty of \endash 4 to the attack roll.
\par \tab In dusty, snowy, or sandy regions, the caster can instead use }{\i\fs24 wind servant }{\fs24 to create a vicious zephyr of stinging dust around an enemy. This zephyr inflicts damage equal to the opponent\rquote 
s base AC less 2d6 points and creates a \endash 2 penalty to the victim\rquote s attack rolls. For example, an enemy in leather armor +1 (AC 7) would suffer 7 \endash  2d6 damage if attacked by means of this spell. Note that any use of the }{\i\fs24 
wind servant }{\fs24 requires the priest\rquote s undivided attention; he can take no other actions while directing the spell.
