\par Sensory: Moderate visual/tactile\tab Critical: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This potent defense surrounds the caster in a chaotic maelstrom of energy and demimatter that blocks or deflects many attacks. The }{\i\fs24 entropy shield }{\fs24 extends about two feet in all directions from the caster\rquote 
s body. The warping effect of the field causes any melee or hand\_to\_hand attack to miss 50% of the time\emdash even if the roll allows an attack to continue, the priest still gains a \endash 
2 bonus to his Armor Class. Normal missiles or hurled weapons miss automatically as the }{\i\fs24 entropy shield }{\fs24 deflects them from the caster. Even magical missile attacks (}{\i\fs24 produce flame, magic missile}{\fs24 , or }{\i\fs24 Melf\rquote 
s acid arrow}{\fs24 , for example), siege engines, and giant\_thrown boulders may be deflected as if they were hand\_to\_hand attacks.
\par \tab Against spells or effects that produce energy, gas, or other physical attack forms (}{\i\fs24 fireball, lightning bolt, cloudkill, }{\fs24 and other such spells) the }{\i\fs24 entropy shield }{\fs24 
provides a 50% chance that the attack simply does not affect the protected priest. Even if the harmful energy or matter penetrates the shield, the caster gains a +2 bonus on his saving throw. This does not cause a spell to fizz
le or fail; a priest standing in the middle of a}{\i\fs24  fireball }{\fs24 
is simply not touched by the spell, which will inflict its normal damage on anyone else in the area of effect. Any spell or effect that does not create matter or energy to harm or hinder the victim can pass through the }{\i\fs24 entropy shield }{\fs24 
normally, so mind\_based attacks and magical effects such as }{\i\fs24 petrification, paralyzation, enfeeblement}{\fs24 , or }{\i\fs24 polymorph }{\fs24 (to name a few) can still affect the priest.
\par \tab In addition to its defensive benefits, the }{\i\fs24 entropy shield }{\fs24 has the ability to repel normal or giant\_
sized animals and creatures of lawful alignment, such as extraplanar monsters from the lawful planes. Any such creature attempting to attack the shielded priest in hand\_to\_hand combat must roll a saving throw vs. sp
ell at the end of the round. If the creature fails, it recoils from the priest and cannot attack him physically for the remainder of the spell\rquote s duration (although it could decide to turn on one of the priest\rquote s companions).
\par \tab The material component for this spell is a gemstone worth at least 100 gold pieces that has been exposed to the chaotic energies of Limbo.
\par 
\par }{\fs28\cf6 Whirlwind
\par }{\b\fs24 (Invocation/Evocation)
\par }{\fs24 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx3240\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\adjustright {\fs24 Sphere: Elemental (Air)
\par Range: 60 yds. + 10 yds./level\tab Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 rd./level\tab Casting Time: 9
\par Area of Effect: Cone 10 ft.\tab Saving Throw: Special
\par   wide at base and 30 ft. tall
\par Subtlety: +6\tab Knockdown: d20
\par Sensory: Huge visual/audio,\tab Critical: Large (1d3
\par   large tactile\tab hits) crushing
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell creates a powerful cyclone of raging wind that moves as directed by the priest. The }{\i\fs24 whirlwind }{\fs24 can move by zigzagging along the ground or over water at a movement rate of 6. The }{\i\fs24 whirlwind }{\fs24 
always moves after all other creatures have moved, and many creatures can avoid it simply by keeping their distance. If the cyclone exceeds the spell\rquote s range, it moves in a random, uncontrolled fashion for 1d3 rounds\emdash 
possibly endangering the caster or his allies\emdash and then dissipates.
\par \tab Any creature of size L (large) or smaller that comes in contact with the }{\i\fs24 whirlwind }{\fs24 must make a saving throw vs. breath weapon or suffer 2d8 damage. Size M (man\_
sized) or smaller creatures who fail their first saving throw must attempt a second one, or be picked up bodily by the }{\i\fs24 whirlwind }{\fs24 
and held suspended in its powerful winds, suffering 1d8 points of damage each round with no save allowed. The caster may direct the cyclone to eject any carried creatures whenever he wishes, depositing the hapless souls wherever the }{\i\fs24 whirlwind }{
\fs24 happens to be when they are released.
\par \tab Maintaining the }{\i\fs24 whirlwind }{\fs24 requires the caster\rquote s full attention, and he cannot cast other spells or make any attacks while directing the spell\rquote 
s course. If his concentration fails for some reason, he cannot simply cancel the spell. Instead, the spell becomes uncontrolled as described above and dissipates after 1d3 rounds.
\par \tab In truly desperate circumstances, priests of elemental air have been known to deliberately overrun their companions in order to carry them out of the path of 
some certain doom. Few care to repeat the experience. The material component for this spell is a handful of dust collected from a zephyr or snow from a williwaw.
\par 
